  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3003.14 Limitation",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3003.14 Limitation.\n\n(a) A person who qualifies for a hardship registration shall be able to obtain a hardship registration for the total number of vehicles on which the person’s name appears on the registration form, if the person requests.\n\n(b) The owner of a vehicle whose license and registration privileges have been suspended or revoked shall not be authorized to operate the vehicle, despite the fact that a hardship registration has been obtained, until his or her license and registration privileges have been restored.\n\nSource. #5027, eff 12-19-90; ss by #6296, eff 7-23-96, EXPIRED: 7-23-04\n\nNew. #8181, eff 9-25-04 (from Saf-C 3003.16); ss by #10085, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13279, eff 10-19-21\n\nAPPENDIX",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3000.html"
